{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/597284-wraith-20-new-spectres-chapter","id":597284,"title":"Wraith 20 New Spectres Chapter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-20T14:01:19-07:00","id":597284,"title":"Wraith 20 New Spectres Chapter","content":"Suprising that nobody posted about this update yet. It has been almost a week since Richard Thomas sent a link to a preview of the Spectres chapter of Wraith 20.<br /> <br /> It looks really cool. I liked how concisely it conveyed so much information, and I liked almost everything new - even if I feel like some powers need clarification.<br /> <br /> Here is the link: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNuOERVNV9SS3N4UGc/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7F...9SS3N4UGc/view</a><br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T17:34:35-07:00","id":597551,"title":"","content":"I like that they changed the former Composure stat of the Psyche to Pathos, and that Spectre Willpower is no longer given an arbitrary alternate name (Being). It's sort of weird to see advice on mechanically putting together Malfeans, but I suppose it might be necessary if, say, characters don't learn from history and try to challenge the Jade Emperor to single combat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:40:42-07:00","id":603898,"title":"","content":"I love it. Here are a few thoughts...<br /> <br /> There are some typos, and under the description of Angst they seem to refer to temporary Angst points as dots and a score on occasion. Across the games, dots/scores usually refer to permanent ratings while squares/points refer to temporary ratings. As the preceding description of spectre creation indicates that spectres have 10 permanent Angst and use the trait as a pool (like Pathos), the mix up is unhelpful (although it's an inconsistency that crops up in all game lines, as M20 also mixed the two up under the description of Willpower). This happens again under the Freebie Points section, where I assume it means you can buy two points of Angst per Freebie, and not two dots. If I'm reading it right, spectres just have an Angst pool and don't have an Angst score (because it's 10).<br /> <br /> Willpower retains the Second Edition price (two Freebies and not one), rather than the Revised cost. I wonder if that's intentional, and if it is, whether Willpower is just more expensive for spectres or if it's more expensive for wraiths too.<br /> <br /> I'm glad botc<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">hes are optional. Especially because the botching rule for corpus would make it very unlikely any characters would survive past a handful of games (I'm also assuming the same rule doesn't hold true for Malfeans, because over thousands of years they'd inevitably rack up a few botches). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Haints and hekatonkhire don't appear, presumably due to space. I'm guessing they'll come in the Book of Oblivion<span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.<br /> <br /> I think</span></span></span> Labyrinth and Shadowlands seem slightly odd as Backgrounds, because they feel more like Knowledges. I can also see the need for Wealth, as some Doppelgangers presumably maintain wraithly wealth (and Yu Huang certainly does). I'd maybe just limit it to Malfeans and Doppelgangers.<br /> <br /> I think it's a very concise and effective section. The order feels a bit backwards, however (I'd have character creation before traits descriptions, for example, to mirror other games). But, to be honest, I'm just so excited for this that none of these minor gripes is really a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:03:38-07:00","id":605180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/597284-wraith-20-new-spectres-chapter?p=603898#post603898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm also assuming the same rule doesn't hold true for Malfeans, because over thousands of years they'd inevitably rack up a few botches).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that to be considered a Malfean you have to have mastery of that Dark Arcanos that lets you bounce Oblivion-caused damage onto other wraiths.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:10:02-07:00","id":606530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/597284-wraith-20-new-spectres-chapter?p=605180#post605180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing that to be considered a Malfean you have to have mastery of that Dark Arcanos that lets you bounce Oblivion-caused damage onto other wraiths.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be it! Good point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is there a mechanic for devouring other beings? I know there's Rapacity, but I don't think that's the same thing. The fluff always mentioned Malfeans devouring other beings to grow their own corpus. Which suggests there's a kind of diablerie for wraiths that Malfeans have mastered. I didn't see it in the excerpt provided, but it is rather long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T09:47:06-07:00","id":628751,"title":"","content":"OK, I haven't been here in a while, but where did you guys see the Spectres chapter preview? I would have thought it would have been sent via the Kickstarter updates and neither my nor any of my compatriots got an update. Hmmm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T11:28:13-07:00","id":628865,"title":"","content":"It went straight into my spam folder when the update went out, but here's the link to link: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-editio/posts/1293864\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/1293864</a><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>